{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/1481072-lfg-looking-for-v20-or-v5-game-that-allows-for-a-7th-generation-elder-pc","id":1481072,"title":"[LFG] Looking for V20 or V5 game that allows for a 7th generation Elder PC","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-14T07:53:31-07:00","id":1481072,"title":"[LFG] Looking for V20 or V5 game that allows for a 7th generation Elder PC","content":"Hello everyone, I am currently looking to join a game (preferably play by post) game that will allow me to play a character concept I have never gotten to play before: an elder. I have played both neonates and fledglings, but have never had the chance to play an elder kindred. This has been a dream of mine to play, but I have never found a ST willing to let me start off as one. This is understandable, because elders are some of the strongest and most powerful characters in any given game.<br /> <br /> I understand that, if given the chance to have an elder PC, it would require a lot of responsibility on my part to correctly portray him and his point of view as being an ancient being who has seen most everything fade and pass on.<br /> <br /> My concept for an elder PC is a Toreador who was embraced in the early 1300s in the Courts of Love in France who managed to survive the ages and various kindred conflicts that arose during his unlife. Instead of playing a character with schemes within schemes, I wanted to play an elder who disguised himself as a neonate or, perhaps, an ancilla, who, while still being a strong player in Camarilla politics, is doing everything he can to hold on to himself and to fight the ennui that slowly consumes elders.<br /> <br /> I have had an idea to actually make him seem youthful and in touch with modern cultural trends, especially being fascinated with video games, streamers, and the internet music scene. I love the idea of the juxtaposition of an ancient being thrust into modern pop culture and trying to adapt so as to hold on to his humanity while also being aware of the greater, darker world at large.<br /> <br /> I want to portray the weight of ages that burden such a character; trying to cope with seeing the world changing to be nearly unrecognizable from the time he was embraced. I want to experience what it is to be an ancient vampire and ask myself questions about what humanity truly means. I also want to experience deep parts of kindred lore and have all of these themes collide in one character, hopefully making someone who is truly memorable.<br /> <br /> I do best when people ask me questions about such a character so that I can elaborate more on him and talk about concepts that I didn't think to mention here.<br /> <br /> If anyone is interested in letting me play such a character in your chronicle, please let me know <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I like to think I'm relatively easy to work with and can make certain adjustments to fit the given chronicle.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2204-toreador","name":"Toreador","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2204_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}